{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on f5cd9e5a (CLI item 3 of 14895240: proof boundary for a room\nother than the register's first).\n\n1. For this head: the qualified missing-dependency result. `dap verify\n--all` from a second room reads the register's entries that the room's\nclaim chain names through its membership session, judges what it can\nreplay in full, and reports the register's founding as a qualified\noutcome that names the exact dependency: the first Directory's genesis\njournal through the register's creation result, and that this room's\nsession is denied that journal (sessions.ts:241-248). The words are\n\"not proven: needs \u003cjournal\u003e entries \u003crange\u003e, not readable by this\nsession\", never \"incomplete\", never \"consistent\". Full replay judgment,\nindependent source-admission proof, exact membership authority and the\nrecorded native bytes stay as they are. No caller anchor is invented, no\nretained copy stands in for a journal page, and no other room's journal\nauthority widens.\n\n2. Not in this head: a bounded genesis proof read. It is a change to the\nread boundary and needs its own design: which prefix (the first\nDirectory's genesis through the register's creation result), who may\nread it (any membership session of a room under that register), its\nbounds, native compatibility and the witness. I will file it as a\nseparate request after this head's evaluation shows how often the\nqualified result occurs. Do not build it under 14895240.\n\n3. A supplied anchor with provenance is acceptable only as an explicit\ninput the CLI records as supplied, with the result labelled as proven\nagainst supplied history. It is not required for this head; leave it\nout unless it already exists.\n\nThe two-room Native witness should exercise this path and record the\nqualified outcome with its exact wording. Cache, truthful 429, finite\nbudgets, late founding, target refusal and unknown-outcome work continue\nunder the original request.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}